Apache Felix Dependency Manager Release Guide
=============================================

This document describes how to release the Dependency Manager with Maven. It is based on the Release FAQ [1]. The
release is made with the Maven release plugin, from this directory.

The bundles in this directory are versioned and released separately: a release only contains the bundles which
changed, and the other bundles stay at the version they were last released with. Like for the other Felix
subprojects, the version in the pom of a bundle is a development version with an odd patch number
(5.0.1-SNAPSHOT), which is released with the next even one (5.0.2).

Prerequisites
=============

* A JDK, 11 or later, and Maven.
* gpg, with a public key added to the KEYS file [2].
* Your Apache credentials in ~/.m2/settings.xml, for the server id apache.releases.https.
* The tags of the repository, which tell what was released before: git fetch origin --tags
* A clean checkout of master, with all the changes you want to release committed and pushed.

Before you start
================

* Make sure there are no dependencies on snapshots or unreleased versions of other modules, apart from the modules
  of this directory.
* Add the release to changelog.txt: the list of the bundles that are part of it, and their issues. Commit it.
* Check that the version in Jira exists, and that the issues of the release are resolved.

Release
=======

  mvn -N exec:exec@release-plan

Run it in a terminal, from this directory. It guides you through the release, and asks for what it needs: you
type an answer and press enter, or just press enter for the answer between the brackets. It:

* checks that the working tree is clean, that you are not behind origin, and fetches the tags: they tell what was
  released before.
* shows, for every bundle, if something changed since the tag of its latest release. It only looks at git: the
  changes in the source of a bundle count, but not the changes of its tests and its documentation. The pom of a
  bundle only counts for the changes that are not about a version: it says so with a bundle that did not change
  otherwise. Check the changes of the modules a bundle depends on before you leave that bundle out. A module that
  is a bundle but does not list the maven-antrun-plugin like the other bundles (see pom.xml) does not take part:
  it warns about it.
* proposes the versions, and asks you to confirm the version of the parent and of every bundle that changed. The
  bundles that did not change are put back to the version that they were released with, and that is also how the
  build knows not to deploy them again (see the apache-release profile in pom.xml).
* warns when changelog.txt does not list the bundles and versions that are released.
* offers a dry run, which builds everything and changes nothing. (The real prepare builds everything too, before
  it commits anything, so the dry run is not needed.)
* runs mvn release:prepare, after you confirmed it. That builds and tests everything, commits the release
  versions, creates the tag dependencymanager-parent-x.y.z for the whole build, commits the next development
  versions, and pushes all that. When it fails it offers to roll back what it changed.
* runs mvn release:perform, after you confirmed it. That builds the tag, signs the artifacts (you will be asked
  for your gpg passphrase), and deploys them to a staging repository on https://repository.apache.org. Only the
  parent pom and the bundles that changed are deployed: a bundle whose version has been released before is
  skipped. Every bundle that is deployed is also tagged with its own tag, <artifactId>-<version>, for example
  org.apache.felix.dependencymanager-5.0.2, and the tag is pushed.

Every step that changes something asks first, and nothing that is not answered is done: without a terminal the
release stops. The commands it runs are shown, so you can run them yourself, too: with

  mvn -N exec:exec@release-plan -Dplan.only=true

it only prints the proposal and the mvn release:prepare command with the options for the versions
(-Dproject.rel.<groupId>:<artifactId>=... and -Dproject.dev....), and changes nothing. Run that command, and then
mvn release:perform.

The source release is the file dependencymanager-parent-x.y.z-source-release.zip: it holds the whole directory,
so also the bundles which are not part of this release.

A bundle is tagged right after it was deployed. When the perform fails halfway, drop the staging repository
and run mvn release:perform again: a tag on the commit that is being released is not taken for a release of
an earlier time, so the bundles that were deployed before the failure are deployed again. (A tag on another
commit is a bundle that was released before, and it is skipped.) No tag is made for a snapshot version.

Log in to https://repository.apache.org, check that the staging repository holds what you expect (the pom, jar,
sources, javadoc, and the signature and checksums of each), and close it. The id of the repository (for example
1560 for orgapachefelix-1560) is used below.

Voting on the release
=====================

Start a vote on the dev@felix.apache.org list, for example:

>>>
To: "Felix Developers List" <dev@felix.apache.org>
Subject: [VOTE] Release Apache Felix Dependency Manager 5.0.2

Hi,

I would like to call for a vote on the following Dependency Manager release:

  org.apache.felix.dependencymanager 5.0.2

We solved N issues in this release:
https://issues.apache.org/jira/projects/FELIX/versions/...

Staging repository:
https://repository.apache.org/content/repositories/orgapachefelix-<id>

You can use this UNIX script to download the release and verify the signatures:
https://github.com/apache/felix-dev/blob/master/check_staged_release.sh

Usage:
  sh check_staged_release.sh <id> /tmp/felix-staging

Please vote to approve this release:

  [ ] +1 Approve the release
  [ ] -1 Don't approve the release (please provide specific comments)

This vote will be open for 72 hours.
<<<

Promoting the release
=====================

When the vote has passed:

* Release the staging repository on https://repository.apache.org, which publishes it to Maven Central.
* Copy the source release and the jars, with their signatures and checksums, to the release area
  https://dist.apache.org/repos/dist/release/felix, and remove the superseded ones.
* Update the downloads page and the news of the website, and mark the versions as released in Jira.
* Announce the release on the dev@ and users@ lists.

Cancelling the release
======================

* Drop the staging repository on https://repository.apache.org.
* Delete the tags that were created: dependencymanager-parent-x.y.z and the tag of every bundle that was
  deployed, locally and on origin (git push origin --delete <tag>).
* Fix the problem, and prepare the release again.

[1] http://www.apache.org/dev/release.html
[2] http://www.apache.org/dist/felix/KEYS
